& [SchemaReferenceClosure] scans each residual_ids set in the five CanonicalMachineSchemaDocument records inside the exact I02 bundle payload documents map
  + standalone schema JSON payloads intentionally omit this metadata and are not residual-reference sources
  + every encountered id resolves to exactly one record
  + current references are RMS-R01 through RMS-R06
  + registry-only successor records remain valid but are not misrepresented as document citations

& [Indexes] are derived by root subject type disposition stage module function and proof reference
  + every value is a sorted unique residual-id vector
  + rebuild from records must exactly equal stored indexes
  + records remain authoritative when an index is absent corrupt or stale

& [RegistryDigest] uses versioned length-prefixed canonical encoding and SHA256
  + binds domain profile parent I03 UUID I02 bundle byte length file digest embedded payload digest embedded exact-baseline fingerprint ordered snapshots records and indexes
  + file digest payload digest and baseline fingerprint are integrity identities and are not misrepresented as digital signatures
  + excludes timestamps human line locators and display formatting

& [Query] is deterministic pure exact and non-executing
  + returns query digest matched ids and exact records
  + never returns a function pointer callback mutable authority token or inferred satisfaction

& [FutureSourceTouch] is unsigned and exact
  + modify crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs only after feature-policy activation
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/residual_registry.rs
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/residual_registry.rs
  - never: current enforcement schema golden Cargo dependency core CLI MCP service ecosystem preflight provider model effect or hardware file

& [Proof] after future activation covers exact 20-record order field closure id grammar source digest staleness schema-reference closure every index reconstruction query determinism record snapshots dispositions policies and mutation refusal
  + exact source-snapshot recomputation
  + exact bundle identity 247809 bytes SHA256 03616F46C4A3C4B7FA4B9D0A668E16FF4B47BA71CB70879B10F1D95157ADCB42 and six residual ids in each of five document records
  + missing duplicate unknown reordered and stale record cases
  + positive and empty query intersections
  + proof that queries never invoke bound functions
  + complete locked offline debug release formatting lint docs audit evidence and diff gates

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + current slice adds source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof narrative and evidence metadata only
  - never: Rust registry parser validator serde invocation semantic admission compatibility provider model service persistence network effect production hardware or FPGA

& [PresentDisposition] is formed_not_activated
